        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior is the 2024-01 to 2026-05 DGORDER MoM base rate mean of +0.47 pp. I add +1.3 pp for transport/aircraft rebound after May's -14.0 percent transportation drop and June Boeing order strength, +0.4 pp for ISM new orders at 56.0, subtract 0.2 pp for flat Fed manufacturing output, and subtract 0.2 pp for softer exports/prices drag, giving +1.8 percent. Interval method uses realized dispersion of DGORDER MoM values themselves: sigma = 5.15, so 80 percent half-width is roughly 1.28*sigma = 1.28*5.15 = 6.59 pp; +1.8 +/- 6.6 gives [-4.8, 8.4] after rounding."
